arm64: dts: h713: hy300-pro - the focus motor's tables from its own stock tree

The HY300 Pro of issue #1 includes sun50i-h713-hy310.dts and so got the
HY310's focus motor: PH4..PH7, limiter PH14, and the HY310's half-step
tables. Its own stock tree (the owner's boot package, analysis A14) enables
motor_ctr on the same pins with other tables - cw 09 08 0c 04 06 02 03 01,
ccw 01 03 02 06 04 0c 08 09, phase delay 5, step delay 2 - and its stock
boot log prints those tables. They energise the four lines in another
order (PH4, PH7, PH6, PH5 where the HY310 goes PH4, PH7, PH5, PH6): the
HY310's sequence is not the one his firmware drives. The node takes his
tables and delays; pins, limiter and the rest stay. The limiter's level is
not in his tree; the HY310's active_level 1 stays, his boots of 16.09.2026
read the limiter 1 (in range), and homing at probe moves only when it
reads out of range.

The lamp's PWM words were already here (0166, 0166a) and stay; their comment
now says they go by address (0168) and that their effect on the picture is
open. The power key is PL4, as his stock gpio_keys say. PB5 hog, PH17
tacho and the disabled pwm-backlight are unchanged.

DTB (host cpp + dtc, kbuild's flags; the "before" DTB equals the tree's
kbuild one byte for byte): decompiled, the diff is motor-cw-table,
motor-ccw-table, motor-phase-udelay and motor-step-mdelay, nothing else.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
@@ -4,10 +4,10 @@
  *
  * The hardware description lives in sun50i-h713-hy310.dts; this
  * board carries its own name so that the DTB it boots is not named after
- * somebody else's board. Focus motor and power key are assumed to sit
- * where the HY310 has them; its owner tests it. The panel is programmed
- * by the display coprocessor from the declared project id (0x34), not by
- * this tree.
+ * somebody else's board. The power key is PL4 as on the HY310 (his stock
+ * gpio_keys; our U-Boot's power gate answers it on his unit). The panel is
+ * programmed by the display coprocessor from the declared project id (0x34),
+ * not by this tree.
  *
  * Two facts from this board's own stock device tree and vendor kernel
  * (19.09.2026, analysis A14): PB5 is the enable of the LED boost AND of
@@ -53,11 +53,12 @@
  * umbau/work/A12 material), and the vendor's PanelControl hands those six
  * numbers to the firmware at start (Thal_Vp_SetBacklightPwmInfo, AP3d
  * 3.5) before it sends the level. The hdmirx driver does the same with
- * allwinner,backlight-pwm-info. Without them the firmware never drives the
- * dimmer and the picture is dark (23.09.2026, the owner's photos against
- * stock at the same exposure). The HY310's ini names channel 2, PB4, which
- * is not wired on that board (cstenger 06.08.2026, A14) - which is why the
- * HY310 was never dark and carries nothing here.
+ * allwinner,backlight-pwm-info, by address since 0168 (sent as six call
+ * parameters, 0166, the channel number was read as an address and memory
+ * was corrupted). Whether they brighten this board's picture is open: the
+ * HY300PRO-G-EU's dull picture was 6-bit LVDS (U-Boot 2de0cc8). The
+ * HY310's ini names channel 2, PB4, which is not wired on that board
+ * (cstenger 06.08.2026, A14), so the HY310 carries nothing here.
  *
  * No pin group for it: the vendor's pwm5@2000c15 node names no pins, and
  * PA12 (vendor pwm4, our pinctrl table's pwm4 on mux 2) is the AC200
@@ -70,3 +71,19 @@
 &hdmirx {
 	allwinner,backlight-pwm-info = <5 1 40000 1 1 100>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * The focus motor as this board's stock tree has it (motor_ctr "okay", his
+ * stock boot log prints the same tables): PH4..PH7 and limiter PH14 as on
+ * the HY310, but its own half-step tables - its coil order is not the
+ * HY310's, whose tables the include brings - and its own delays (read as
+ * ms by this driver, as the HY310's stock reads them). The limiter's level
+ * is not in his tree; the HY310's active_level 1 stays (his boots of 16.09.
+ * read it 1, in range).
+ */
+&motor_ctr {
+	motor-cw-table = [09 08 0C 04 06 02 03 01];
+	motor-ccw-table = [01 03 02 06 04 0C 08 09];
+	motor-phase-udelay = <5>;
+	motor-step-mdelay = <2>;
+};
